# Repository-root ignores.
#
# Scope: this file covers noise that can land anywhere in the superproject —
# OS turds, editor state, Python tool caches and local secrets. It deliberately
# does NOT restate the Godot project's own rules; those live in
# godot-base/.gitignore, next to the project.godot they describe.
#
# Note that these rules do not reach inside the submodules listed in
# .gitmodules (anti_checkers, anti_chess, chicken_pit, dead_metal_jam,
# lazer_nfc). A submodule is its own repository with its own index, so it
# carries its own .gitignore. Plain game folders under godot-base/games/
# (desk_can_saw, triangle_rush) are part of this repository and are covered.

# Godot engine caches — a safety net, not a duplicate.
# godot-base/.gitignore already covers the host project, but a game folder
# opened directly in the editor writes these beside its own files, and a
# reimport run from an unexpected working directory can drop one at the root.
.godot/
.import/
*.translation
mono_crash.*.json

# Per-machine engine overrides. Godot reads an override.cfg beside
# project.godot to patch project settings locally; committing one would hand
# every other clone somebody's private renderer or window setup.
override.cfg

# Export output. Presets are tracked on purpose (see godot-base/.gitignore),
# but the binaries they produce are not.
/exports/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.pck

# Signing material and other local secrets. AGENTS.md requires keystore paths
# and passwords to stay in the editor's per-machine settings rather than in the
# tracked export_presets.cfg; this makes a slip harder to commit by accident.
*.keystore
*.jks
export_credentials.cfg
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python tooling under */tools/ (render_audio.py, measure_intro_cues.py,
# render_cover.gd's companions). Standard library only, so there is nothing to
# lock — just interpreter and cache droppings.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editor and IDE state.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Scratch output: crash dumps and stray local logs. Recorded assets and
# generated covers are committed with their sources, so nothing here should
# shadow them.
*.stackdump
*.tmp
*.bak
